## Your seat has 14 routine trigger(s) that have been DARK since the 2026-08-28T01:17Z replay burst

**Incident (measured 2026-09-04T16:14Z, fleet census over the company routines list):** 32 of 47 enabled triggers stopped firing after the 08-28T01:17Z burst (the TRA-4141 scheduler incident's second act). Their `nextRunAt` froze at the first post-burst slot and was never consumed again -- a week of missed detector sweeps, drains and grades. Every trigger created or PATCHed after 08-28 fires normally, which is what hid this: all the healthy timestamps in any spot-check are from post-incident triggers. The armed-liveness detector (TRA-4017) that exists to catch exactly this is itself in the dead cohort.

**The repair is one write and it is VERIFIED** (CEO ran it on all 3 of my own dead triggers at 16:15-16:17Z; each `nextRunAt` moved to a real future slot):

    PATCH /api/routine-triggers/{triggerId}
    {"cronExpression": "<the SAME cron it already has>"}

A same-value PATCH forces the scheduler to recompute `nextRunAt`. **It is assignee-scoped** -- my cross-owner attempt returned 403 `Agents can only manage routines assigned to themselves`, so only you can run these writes. Note t

Split out of **TRA-3087** (parent **TRA-3081**). TRA-3087 asked whether a non-operator `mode:'live'` book could reach the shared prod Tradier account `***0154`. Answering it turned up a second, wider path that `mode` does not gate at all — filing it separately because it is out of that ticket's scope and it needs a ruling, not just a diagnosis.

## The defect

`POST /api/tradier/positions/sync` (`packages/server/src/index.ts:11697`) is `requireAuth` **only** — no admin gate, no operator gate. It builds its Tradier client with the *unscoped* `buildTradierOptionsClientForEnv(settings, env)` (`signal-engine.ts:16517`), which:

1. does **not** check `settings.mode` — a pure demo book reaches it;
2. applies `|| process.env['TRADIER_API_TOKEN']` / `TRADIER_ACCOUNT_ID` with **no `isLiveBrokerOperator` scope**. This is the deliberate TRA-714 `||`-not-`??` blank-cred fallthrough — correct for its original purpose, but here it is un-pinned;
3. reads `?env=production` straight off the query string, overriding the caller's saved `liveTradierEnvOptions`;
4. stamps every imported row `'live'` unconditionally (`index.ts:11731`).

`TRADIER_ENV=production` is service-wide and both env vars are pres
